WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.601 --> 00:00:03.136
-My first guest tonight is one
of the biggest names in music.

00:00:03.136 --> 00:00:07.039
She is a Grammy winner
who's had four number-one songs

00:00:07.039 --> 00:00:08.808
on the Billboard Hot 100.

00:00:08.808 --> 00:00:11.444
Her latest single, "Up,"
has already gone up

00:00:11.444 --> 00:00:14.180
to number one
on Apple Music and iTunes.

00:00:14.180 --> 00:00:18.150
Here is the one and only
Cardi B!

00:00:18.150 --> 00:00:20.219
-Whoo-hoo-hoo!

00:00:20.219 --> 00:00:23.489
-It is so good to see you.
You look fantastic.

00:00:23.489 --> 00:00:25.958
-Thank you.
-The last time

00:00:25.958 --> 00:00:29.462
I think we were here together,
we co-hosted the show.

00:00:29.462 --> 00:00:32.097
And you had baby -- you were
still pregnant with baby,

00:00:32.097 --> 00:00:35.668
and now you have a little
1 1/2-year-old running around.

00:00:35.668 --> 00:00:37.937
-Thank you.
I can't wait --

00:00:37.937 --> 00:00:39.739
Are we gonna host --

00:00:39.739 --> 00:00:42.142
When the world
is back open again,

00:00:42.142 --> 00:00:43.443
I want to host your show
again with you.

00:00:43.443 --> 00:00:45.444
That was so fun.
-You were fantastic,

00:00:45.444 --> 00:00:47.580
and, honestly,
it's an open invitation.

00:00:47.580 --> 00:00:49.715
Come back whenever you want to,
please.

00:00:49.715 --> 00:00:53.386
I got to meet that baby.
-For sure.

00:00:53.386 --> 00:00:56.155
-You've had a very busy
past few months.

00:00:56.155 --> 00:00:58.724
In August,
you released the song "WAP,"

00:00:58.724 --> 00:01:01.427
and it became one of
the biggest songs of the year.

00:01:01.427 --> 00:01:04.664
And it had one of our pals
on there, Megan Thee Stallion.

00:01:04.664 --> 00:01:06.699
How did the song come together,
and was --

00:01:06.699 --> 00:01:09.802
was the plan always
to have her on it?

00:01:09.802 --> 00:01:13.706
-Well, I wanted a couple
of girls in the song.

00:01:13.706 --> 00:01:15.441
You know when you have ideas,

00:01:15.441 --> 00:01:18.378
like, "I want to have this
and that girl in the song,"

00:01:18.378 --> 00:01:21.647
I really wanted to have Megan,
but I didn't know her that well.

00:01:21.647 --> 00:01:23.750
And our stylists linked us up,

00:01:23.750 --> 00:01:25.384
and when our stylists
linked us up,

00:01:25.384 --> 00:01:28.721
we kicked it off really well.
And I said, "Oh, girl, I got --

00:01:28.721 --> 00:01:29.922
We'll just say,
I got a song for you."

00:01:29.922 --> 00:01:31.123
"Well, I got a song for you."

00:01:31.123 --> 00:01:33.193
And she loved my song,
and she hopped on it,

00:01:33.193 --> 00:01:36.396
and we made "herstory."
♪ Herstory ♪

00:01:36.396 --> 00:01:38.531
-You've made "herstory."
Oh, my gosh.

00:01:38.531 --> 00:01:39.799
You did, you crushed it.

00:01:39.799 --> 00:01:42.302
She is super-duper fun,
by the way.

00:01:42.302 --> 00:01:44.236
-She is.
-Your new song, "Up,"

00:01:44.236 --> 00:01:46.272
came out last week.
Congrats on this.

00:01:46.272 --> 00:01:48.307
Already number one.

00:01:48.307 --> 00:01:50.976
After "WAP," did you go like --

00:01:50.976 --> 00:01:53.479
Do you get pressure
to put out another song?

00:01:53.479 --> 00:01:54.781
Do you go like,
"I don't want to do it.

00:01:54.781 --> 00:01:56.783
I already scored"?

00:01:56.783 --> 00:01:59.486
-Yeah, I do feel pressure,
but then I feel, like,

00:01:59.486 --> 00:02:02.054
pressure from my fans,
like, "All right.

00:02:02.054 --> 00:02:04.157
We want another --
We want another song."

00:02:04.157 --> 00:02:06.158
-Ready.
-So the pressure

00:02:06.158 --> 00:02:08.361
was even more big
because I haven't released

00:02:08.361 --> 00:02:11.431
a solo single in like two years.

00:02:11.431 --> 00:02:14.033
So I was like, "Oh, my God,
I just want to go top 10."

00:02:14.033 --> 00:02:16.335
And it's predicted
to go probably number 2

00:02:16.335 --> 00:02:19.438
on the Billboard Hot 100.

00:02:19.438 --> 00:02:21.274
So I'm like, "Oh, wow.
I exceeded my limit."

00:02:21.274 --> 00:02:23.776
I'm extremely happy.
-Oh, fantastic.

00:02:23.776 --> 00:02:25.044
I love it.
It's, like, up.

00:02:25.044 --> 00:02:27.646
And then, "If it's up,
then it's stuck"...

00:02:27.646 --> 00:02:28.815
-Yeah.
-...I'd never heard before,

00:02:28.815 --> 00:02:31.818
but that's -- Did Offset --
Is that who --

00:02:31.818 --> 00:02:34.687
I heard that he had something
to do with that phrase?

00:02:34.687 --> 00:02:36.089
-Well, he says that a lot.

00:02:36.089 --> 00:02:37.857
I don't know if
it's a down South thing.

00:02:37.857 --> 00:02:40.126
Because after the song came out,

00:02:40.126 --> 00:02:41.860
I thought it was, like,
a Georgia thing,

00:02:41.860 --> 00:02:43.997
but then people would say,
"Ah, no, we say that

00:02:43.997 --> 00:02:46.699
in New Orleans.
We say that in Florida."

00:02:46.699 --> 00:02:50.803
I'm like, "Okay, man, listen.
All right, I guess, whatever."

00:02:50.803 --> 00:02:52.505
-"You got it. It's yours,
it's yours, whatever."

00:02:52.505 --> 00:02:54.540
-"It's yours."
[ Both laugh ]

00:02:54.540 --> 00:02:57.843
-But if it's --
if it's up, then it's stuck.

00:02:57.843 --> 00:03:01.681
-Yeah.
-What does that mean?

00:03:01.681 --> 00:03:03.115
-Um...

00:03:03.115 --> 00:03:06.351
So, have you ever
taken a poop, right?

00:03:06.351 --> 00:03:09.355
-Hmm.
-And it don't come out?

00:03:09.355 --> 00:03:14.327
-Mm-hmm.
-It's just up, and it's stuck.

00:03:14.327 --> 00:03:16.296
-Okay.

00:03:16.296 --> 00:03:20.066
-Yeah.

00:03:20.066 --> 00:03:22.735
-Wow.

00:03:22.735 --> 00:03:24.437
All right.
I mean, I guess you could

00:03:24.437 --> 00:03:26.238
take from it whatever you want,
you know?

00:03:26.238 --> 00:03:30.643
There's other...you know,
ways to look at it, I guess.

00:03:30.643 --> 00:03:32.111
-Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:03:32.111 --> 00:03:36.315
I was saying, if it's up,
that it's up here forever.

00:03:36.315 --> 00:03:39.852
Once you get up...
[ Whistles ]

00:03:39.852 --> 00:03:44.724
-It got -- It's a metaphor --
a metaphorical quote.

00:03:44.724 --> 00:03:46.592
-Right? Yeah.
-[ Laughs ]

00:03:46.592 --> 00:03:48.494
You're floating, you're up,
and you're stuck up,

00:03:48.494 --> 00:03:50.663
and good for you, because
you worked hard to get up,

00:03:50.663 --> 00:03:52.865
and it's stuck,
and now there you go.

00:03:52.865 --> 00:03:55.835
-Yeah, stuck.
-[ Laughs ]

00:03:55.835 --> 00:03:58.470
-There's two -- There's
different ways to look at it.

00:03:58.470 --> 00:04:00.840
"Up" is already awesome.

00:04:00.840 --> 00:04:04.510
Is there a new album on the way?
Can we say anything or no?

00:04:04.510 --> 00:04:07.746
-Um, I really want
my next project

00:04:07.746 --> 00:04:11.017
